diff --git a/docs/development/credit-capacity-contract.md b/docs/development/credit-capacity-contract.md
index b6ed7a8..8e2df5b 100644
--- a/docs/development/credit-capacity-contract.md
+++ b/docs/development/credit-capacity-contract.md
@@ -310,3 +310,31 @@ commercial acceptance (including live browser qualification) is evidenced.
 Those remaining financial interfaces require coordinator review before their
 implementation; they are explicit next gates, not reasons to duplicate already
 implemented ordinary allocation/refund workflows or remove scope.
+
+### Unqualified commitment-witness prerequisite (3 November 2026)
+
+A payment event's `created_at` is its insertion time, not its transaction's commit
+clock. It cannot prove that cash committed before the inclusive UTC cutoff. The
+unfinished witness candidate therefore observes an already visible native payment
+or allocation in a fresh server transaction after the posting transaction has
+finished, validates its source/journal/posting-effect identities and records a
+server-clock receipt. A receipt created on a late retry stays late. A later
+receipt commit does not change the fact that the source was already committed at
+the observation clock. Both the payment and its qualifying allocation need this
+proof; agreement binding also needs a separately reviewed committed-observation
+boundary before either event. No client clock or insertion timestamp substitutes.
+
+This candidate does not enable conditional terms, evidence capture, agreement
+binding, conditional-credit admission or redeemed-allocation protection. Its
+review SQL is not registered or installed. The optional observer preserves an
+already committed payment outcome when unavailable; eligibility must eventually
+read and validate the persisted receipt, never trust that response status.
+
+The fresh-transaction service boundary is implemented. The draft SQL's direct
+same-transaction `xmin` check is only a partial defense: subtransactions, XID
+wraparound and frozen rows are not qualified. Before integration, require actual
+disposable PostgreSQL tests for parent/savepoint inserts, concurrent invisible
+rows and commit/rollback, delayed cutoff crossings, exact retries, immutable
+permissions, partial schema and source tampering. Mocked service tests are not
+commit-visibility evidence. No existing database or production activation is
+permitted by this candidate, and all earlier P01-03 acceptance gates remain.
